 NDT expertise across multiple inspection methods. API (American Petroleum Institute) certifications focus on specific equipment and industry applications—API 570 for piping, API 653 for tanks, and API 510 for pressure vessels. Most professionals hold both ASNT and API certifications."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3","children":"How long does it take to prepare for certification exams?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600","children":"Most candidates require 3-6 months of dedicated study, depending on their experience level and the certification chosen. ASNT Level III typically requires the most preparation time due to its comprehensive scope. Many professionals use formal training programs to accelerate their preparation."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3","children":"What's the pass rate for NDT certification exams?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600","children":"Pass rates vary by certification. ASNT Level III typically has a 40-50% first-attempt pass rate due to its difficulty. API certifications generally have higher pass rates of 60-75% with proper preparation. Success requires adequate study time and understanding of technical content."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3","children":"Do certifications expire and require renewal?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-slate-600","children":"ASNT Level III certification is valid for 5 years and requires renewal through re-examination. API certifications typically last 5-6 years and require continuing education or re-examination for renewal. Staying current with your certifications maintains your professional cre